This chapter specifies how the parts of the Morloc ecosystem fit together:
the compiler, the runtime library, the nexus, and the environment manager
`mim`. It defines where each part is installed, how the runtime is built,
how an `import` finds a module, how a program's foreign packages are solved
into an environment, how a compiled program is served to other programs and
agents, and how an environment is frozen into a portable image. The
<<apis>> chapter shows how to use these tools; this chapter specifies what
they do.

This chapter and the two that follow are written as a specification. They
describe behavior, formats and guarantees rather than any particular
implementation, so they should remain true of any conforming
reimplementation.

